set -eu
# A two-hour gap the host accounts for: the Mac was asleep for all but fifty seconds of it at a
# stretch, which is under the two intervals a tick needs, so there was no tick to run. The event is
# written with `channel: ["record"]` and **no Mac message is raised** — `calls.log` carries no
# osascript line and no applet launch, which is the whole acceptance.
#
# The status below it is the second half: the tick has just written a new marker, so the live gap
# line is gone, and the record is the only place this outage is ever seen. A gap nobody was told
# about that also disappeared from the view would be worse than the message it replaced.
"$BATON" tick
echo
"$BATON" status
